events.content:
Now I'll design the widget. Architecture:

```
src/
  widget/
    types.ts          — unified API: ChartMode, ChartSeries, TimeSeriesPoint, ChartWidgetProps, ChartEngineComponent props
    ChartWidget.tsx   — the widget: header (title + SegmentedRadioGroup toggle), lazy engine loading via React.lazy + Suspense, legend handling per engine? Legend in engines.
    loadEngine.ts     — mode → () => import(...) with cached lazy components
    engines/
      sales/SalesLineChart.tsx      — SVG line chart, simple, crosshair+tooltip
      monitoring/MonitoringChart.tsx — Canvas dense time series, decimation, crosshair+tooltip, legend
    palette.css or tokens in a style — series colors from validated palette
  data/
    sampleData.ts     — sales data (12 months, maybe 2 series: выручка, заказы? keep sales single series "Продажи" to avoid legend need? Actually 2 series shows legend. Sales: 1 series → no legend. Monitoring: 3 series → legend.)
  App.tsx             — demo: page with widget
```

Unified API:

```ts
export type ChartMode = 'sales' | 'monitoring';

export interface TimeSeriesPoint { t: number; v: number }
export interface ChartSeries { id: string; name: string; color?: string; points: TimeSeriesPoint[] }

export interface ChartEngineProps {
  series: ChartSeries[];
  height: number;
  yUnit?: string;         // suffix for values
  formatValue?: (v:number)=>string;
  formatTime?: (t:number)=>string;
}

export interface ChartWidgetProps extends ChartEngineProps {
  mode: ChartMode;
  onModeChange?: (mode: ChartMode) => void;
  title?: string;
  showModeSwitch?: boolean;
}
```

Lazy loading: React.lazy per mode:
```ts
const engines: Record<ChartMode, React.LazyExoticComponent<React.ComponentType<ChartEngineProps>>> = {
  sales: lazy(() => import('./engines/sales/SalesLineChart')),
  monitoring: lazy(() => import('./engines/monitoring/MonitoringChart')),
};
```
Vite will code-split these into separate chunks. Suspense fallback: spinner (Gravity UI Loader).

Mode switcher: Gravity UI `SegmentedRadioGroup` with options "Продажи" / "Мониторинг".

Engines both accept the same `ChartEngineProps` — that's the unified API.

Palette: use validated palette. Slots used: sales = slot 1 blue #2a78d6 (single series). Monitoring: 3 series → slots 1,2,3 (#2a78d6, #eb6834, #1baf7a). Adjacent pairs pass. Surface: Gravity UI light theme surface is white-ish. Gravity's `--g-color-base-background` is white. I'll run validator with the palette on white surface.

Actually let me run the validator script for ["#2a78d6","#eb6834","#1baf7a"] light mode surface #ffffff (Gravity surface is #fff). The built-in default surface is #fcfcfb; fine, I'll pass --surface #ffffff.

Sales chart (SVG):
- margins, y gridlines (hairline #e1e0d9), x labels (months), 2px line, area fill 10% opacity, end-dot with 2px surface ring, direct label at end (last value), crosshair vertical hairline on hover + tooltip listing series values, tabular-nums for axis ticks.
- Single series → no legend.

Monitoring chart (Canvas):
- thousands of points; canvas 2d render with devicePixelRatio; min-max decimation per pixel column to preserve spikes; crosshair + tooltip on pointermove; legend with 3 series (swatches as line keys); recessive grid.
- Also keep an overlay for tooltip: absolutely positioned div.

Also accessibility: table view toggle. To keep scope manageable, I'll add a "Таблица" toggle in the widget that shows a table of data (sampled for monitoring — every Nth point, or first/last?). Hmm — the skill says "a table view exists". For dense monitoring data, a table of 2000 rows is heavy; I can show decimated rows (e.g., every 10 minutes / sampled to ~50 rows). I'll implement a shared DataTable component in widget that samples to at most ~100 rows.

Modes have different titles: "Продажи по месяцам" vs "Мониторинг инфраструктуры". Widget title prop or auto per mode.

